{
    "metadata": {
        "description": """
Rail transport multi-agent system for nttd/OpenTTD.
LLM agents make strategic decisions (route selection, engine choice,
retry-vs-abandon). Coded tools handle mechanical execution (HTTP calls,
action assembly, observation parsing). Actions flow via sly_data.
""",
        "tags": ["nttd", "openttd", "rail", "transport"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Build a profitable rail cargo route.",
            "What are the best unserved cargo routes?",
            "Connect two industries with a rail line."
        ]
    },
    "llm_config": {
        "model_name": "gpt-5.4"
    },
    "tools": [
        // ==================================================================
        // FRONT MAN: rail_coordinator
        // Calls doctor -> planner -> validator in sequence each cycle.
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "rail_coordinator",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I am a rail transport coordinator for an OpenTTD game.
Give me the current game observation and I will build profitable rail cargo
routes. I call the doctor, planner, and validator in sequence each cycle.
Actions are delivered automatically via sly_data.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "What to do this cycle"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the rail coordinator. Every cycle, follow these steps in order:

1. Call route_doctor to diagnose issues, add orders to incomplete vehicles,
   and retry failed builds.
2. Call route_completer to build depots and buy vehicles for routes that
   have stations and track but no vehicle yet.
3. Call route_planner to select the next route and queue station + track
   build actions. SKIP this step if there are already 3+ active routes
   and none are profitable yet -- focus on completing existing routes first.
4. Call action_validator to validate and deduplicate the action list.

CRITICAL RULES:
- Actions flow through sly_data automatically via coded tools.
- Do NOT add your own actions or modify the action list directly.
- NEVER construct raw build_rail_station, connect_rail, build_train, or
  build_rail_depot actions yourself. Always use the coded tools.
- Only build simple 2-station routes (producer -> consumer, or town -> town).
""",
            "allow": {
                "to_upstream": {
                    "sly_data": ["action_list", "plan_summary"]
                },
                "from_downstream": {
                    "sly_data": ["action_list", "plan_summary"]
                }
            },
            "tools": ["route_doctor", "route_completer", "route_planner", "action_validator", "company_status"]
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // LLM AGENT: route_doctor
        // Repairs incomplete routes: adds orders, retries failed builds.
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "route_doctor",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Repairs incomplete routes: adds orders to vehicles with < 2 orders,
retries failed build actions from the previous cycle. Initializes the
action list in sly_data. Never touches running trains (2+ orders).
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional context about what needs repair"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the route doctor. You add orders to incomplete vehicles and retry failures.

STEP 1: Call check_vehicle_status to see the current state.

STEP 2: For vehicles with < 2 orders (incomplete, need orders):
  - Call pair_orphan_stations with orphan_station_ids.
  - Match each incomplete vehicle to the nearest station pair by
    comparing the vehicle's (x, y) to the pair's station coordinates.
    A vehicle at (30, 207) belongs to the pair near (30, 207).
  - For each match: call build_repair_actions with vehicle_id,
    src_station_id, dst_station_id.

STEP 3: If there were failed actions from the previous cycle:
  - Call retry_failed_actions to queue retries with adjusted parameters.

NEVER touch running trains (vehicles with 2+ orders). They are working.
build_repair_actions will reject assignments if the station pair already has
a running vehicle. If it returns an error, try a different station pair.
Report: needs_depot_and_vehicle flag, repairs done, retries queued.
""",
            "tools": ["check_vehicle_status", "pair_orphan_stations", "build_repair_actions", "retry_failed_actions"]
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // LLM AGENT: route_completer
        // Builds depot + buys vehicles when stations+track exist but no vehicle.
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "route_completer",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Completes routes that have stations and track but no depot or vehicle yet.
Picks an engine and wagons, finds a depot spot near existing track, and
queues build_rail_depot + build_train actions (engine + wagons atomically).
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Context from route_doctor about what needs completing"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the route completer. You finish routes that have stations and track
but still need a depot and vehicles.

STEP 1: Call check_vehicle_status. If needs_depot_and_vehicle is false,
report "Nothing to complete" and stop.

STEP 2: Call pair_orphan_stations with the orphan_station_ids to find
which station pairs form routes.

STEP 3: Call get_engines (vehicle_type=0). Pick ONE station pair to complete
(the first pair). Do NOT try to complete multiple pairs in one cycle.
  - Pick a locomotive (is_wagon=false): prefer cheaper engines early game.
  - You do NOT need to pick a wagon. build_depot_and_vehicles auto-selects
    the correct wagon based on station cargo data.
  - Use num_wagons=3 (matches platform_length=3).

STEP 4: Estimate cost (engine_price + wagon_price * 3 + 3000 for depot).
Call finance_advisor with estimated_cost. If cannot afford, stop.

STEP 5: Call build_depot_and_vehicles with:
  - station_tile: use one of the orphan_station_tiles values
  - dest_station_tile: use the OTHER orphan_station_tiles value from the pair
  - engine_id, num_wagons (wagon is auto-selected)
  It will skip routes that already have a vehicle (1 train per route,
  no signals yet).

CRITICAL: Complete only 1 depot + 1 train per cycle. Do NOT build multiple
depots or trains. Each route gets exactly 1 train (no signals for passing).

Report what you built and for which station pair.
""",
            "tools": ["check_vehicle_status", "pair_orphan_stations", "build_depot_and_vehicles", "get_engines", "finance_advisor", "find_rail_depot_spot"]
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // LLM AGENT: route_planner
        // Selects next route, picks engine+wagons, queues build actions.
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "route_planner",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Plans route expansion: selects the next unserved cargo route, picks an
engine and wagons, validates station/depot spots, checks finances, and
queues build actions in sly_data.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional context about expansion goals"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the route planner. You select and build new routes (cargo or passenger).
You only build stations and track. Depot and vehicles are handled by
route_completer in the next cycle.

STEP 1: Call find_unserved_routes to see available routes.
  - It returns "routes" (cargo) and "town_routes" (passenger).
  - If both are empty with a reason, report that reason and stop.

STEP 2: Select ONE route to build. Consider:
  - Shorter distance = lower build cost (track cost is ~200/tile)
  - Higher monthly_production = more cargo = more revenue
  - Town/passenger routes are good early revenue sources
  - Only build simple 2-station chains. Never plan multi-step supply chains.
  Build at most 1 route per cycle. Do NOT queue multiple routes.

STEP 3: Call get_engines (vehicle_type=0) to pick:
  - A locomotive (is_wagon=false): cheaper engines are fine early game.
  - You do NOT need to pick a wagon. The wagon will be auto-selected
    to match the route's cargo when route_completer builds the train.

STEP 4: Estimate cost: 2 stations (~8,000 each) + track (~200/tile * distance).
  Call finance_advisor with this estimated_cost.
  If cannot afford, skip and report.

STEP 5: Call build_route_actions with:
  - For cargo routes: source_industry_id, dest_industry_id, engine_id
  - For town/passenger routes: source_town_id, dest_town_id, engine_id

CRITICAL: ALWAYS use the build_route_actions coded tool. NEVER construct
raw build_rail_station or connect_rail actions yourself. The coded tool
validates spots via GS queries and ensures correct station directions.

Report which route you selected and why.
""",
            "tools": ["find_unserved_routes", "build_route_actions", "get_engines", "finance_advisor", "find_station_spot", "get_rail_types"]
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // LLM AGENT: action_validator
        // Reviews action list for safety and correctness.
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "action_validator",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Validates the action list in sly_data: removes duplicates, filters unknown
action types, blocks disruptive actions against running trains.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional context about validation concerns"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the action validator. Review the action list for safety.

Call validate_action_list to run automated checks (dedup, safety, filtering).

Review the results:
- If actions were removed, explain why in your summary.
- If the action list is empty, note this -- it means no work this cycle.
- If there are many retries, flag this as a potential issue.
- If there are disruptive actions blocked, confirm the protection worked.

Report: total validated actions, any removed, any concerns.
""",
            "tools": ["validate_action_list"]
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // LLM AGENT: finance_advisor
        // Evaluates affordability, recommends loans.
        // Shared by route_doctor and route_planner (diamond pattern).
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "finance_advisor",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Financial advisor for the rail company. Checks affordability of planned
actions and recommends loan adjustments when needed.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "estimated_cost": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Estimated cost of the planned actions"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["estimated_cost"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the finance advisor. Other agents call you to check affordability.

Call check_finances with the estimated_cost to see the financial picture.

Decision logic:
- If can_afford is true: report "Affordable, no loan needed."
- If can_afford is false but can_afford_with_loan is true:
  Calculate loan amount: current loan + shortfall, rounded up to nearest 10,000.
  Call set_loan_action with that amount.
  Report "Loan adjusted to <amount>."
- If neither: report "Cannot afford even with max loan. Skip this cycle."

Keep responses to 2-3 lines. The caller needs a quick go/no-go.
""",
            "tools": ["check_finances", "set_loan_action"]
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // CODED TOOLS: route_doctor sub-tools
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "check_vehicle_status",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Returns vehicles needing repair (< 2 orders), orphan station IDs not
visited by any vehicle, and failed actions from the previous cycle.
Also initializes sly_data action_list.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional (reads observation directly)"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.check_vehicle_status.CheckVehicleStatus"
        },
        {
            "name": "pair_orphan_stations",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Pairs orphan stations by Manhattan distance proximity. Returns a list of
{src_id, dst_id, distance} pairs representing likely route endpoints.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "orphan_station_ids": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "items": {"type": "int"},
                            "description": "List of orphan station IDs to pair"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["orphan_station_ids"]
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.pair_orphan_stations.PairOrphanStations"
        },
        {
            "name": "build_repair_actions",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Creates add_order x2 + start_vehicle actions for a vehicle and appends
them to sly_data action_list. Only starts the vehicle if it has cargo
capacity (wagons attached). The vehicle will run between the two stations.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "vehicle_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "ID of the vehicle to repair"
                        },
                        "src_station_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Source station ID for the first order"
                        },
                        "dst_station_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Destination station ID for the second order"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["vehicle_id", "src_station_id", "dst_station_id"]
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.build_repair_actions.BuildRepairActions"
        },
        {
            "name": "retry_failed_actions",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Reads failed actions from the previous cycle and creates retry actions
with adjusted parameters (offset tiles for stations, new spot search for
depots). Appends retries to sly_data action_list.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional (reads previous_actions from observation)"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.retry_failed_actions.RetryFailedActions"
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // CODED TOOL: route_completer sub-tool
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "build_depot_and_vehicles",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Finds a depot spot adjacent to existing track near the given station tile,
builds the depot, and buys an engine with wagons atomically attached.
Reuses existing depots when possible. Requires track to already exist.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "station_tile": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Tile ID of a station near which to search for a depot spot"
                        },
                        "dest_station_tile": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Tile ID of the other station in the pair (for duplicate-vehicle check and depot placement)"
                        },
                        "engine_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Locomotive engine ID to purchase"
                        },
                        "wagon_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Wagon engine ID for cargo capacity"
                        },
                        "num_wagons": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Number of wagons to attach (default 3)"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["station_tile", "engine_id"]
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.build_depot_and_vehicles.BuildDepotAndVehicles"
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // CODED TOOLS: route_planner sub-tools
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "find_unserved_routes",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Returns unserved cargo routes and town/passenger routes not near existing
stations. Allows expansion once at least one vehicle is running with orders.
Blocks expansion if 3+ routes exist and none are profitable. Returns:
"routes" (cargo) and "town_routes" (passenger) with coordinates and details.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional (reads observation directly)"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.find_unserved_routes.FindUnservedRoutes"
        },
        {
            "name": "build_route_actions",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Validates station spots via HTTP and builds the complete action sequence
for a new route: 2 stations + track. Supports both cargo routes (by
industry ID) and passenger routes (by town ID). Depot and vehicles are
handled by route_completer in the next cycle.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "source_industry_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Source industry ID (for cargo routes)"
                        },
                        "dest_industry_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Destination industry ID (for cargo routes)"
                        },
                        "source_town_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Source town ID (for passenger routes)"
                        },
                        "dest_town_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Destination town ID (for passenger routes)"
                        },
                        "engine_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Locomotive engine ID to purchase"
                        },
                        "wagon_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Wagon engine ID for cargo capacity"
                        },
                        "num_wagons": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Number of wagons to attach (default 3)"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["engine_id"]
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.build_route_actions.BuildRouteActions"
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // CODED TOOLS: finance_advisor sub-tools
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "check_finances",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Returns company financial status: balance, loan, max_loan, income,
loan_room, and affordability assessment for a given estimated_cost.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "estimated_cost": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Estimated cost to check affordability against"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.check_finances.CheckFinances"
        },
        {
            "name": "set_loan_action",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Creates a set_loan action and prepends it to sly_data action_list.
The loan action must execute before any spending actions.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "amount": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "New loan amount (must be <= max_loan)"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["amount"]
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.set_loan_action.SetLoanAction"
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // CODED TOOL: action_validator sub-tool
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "validate_action_list",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Deduplicates the action list, filters unknown action types, and blocks
disruptive actions (send_to_depot, remove_order) against running trains
(vehicles with 2+ orders). Writes validated list back to sly_data.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional (reads sly_data directly)"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.validate_action_list.ValidateActionList"
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // CODED TOOL: company_status (diagnostic, kept from original)
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "company_status",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Returns a lightweight summary of the company state for decision-making:
game date, company financials (balance, loan, income, profit), station count,
vehicle count with order/speed info, existing routes with profit, orphan
station detection, action history (last 15 cycles), and previous action results.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "detail_level": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Level of detail (default 'full')"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.read_company_status.ReadCompanyStatus"
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // CODED TOOLS: HTTP query tools
        // Called internally by build_route_actions, build_depot_and_vehicles,
        // and retry_failed_actions via nttd_client.query_gs().
        // ==================================================================
        {
            "name": "find_station_spot",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Finds validated rail station spots near an industry or town.
Checks flat land, station buildability (dry-run), and cargo catchment.
Returns tiles where a rail station can be successfully built.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "industry_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Industry ID to find station spots near"
                        },
                        "town_id": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Town ID to find station spots near"
                        },
                        "platform_length": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Station platform length (default 3)"
                        },
                        "rail_type": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Rail type ID (default 0)"
                        },
                        "radius": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Search radius in tiles (default 15)"
                        },
                        "max_results": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Maximum results to return (default 5)"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.find_station_spot.FindStationSpot"
        },
        {
            "name": "find_rail_depot_spot",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Finds tiles adjacent to existing rail track where a depot can be built.
MUST be called AFTER connect_rail so track exists.
Returns tile, x, y, and depot_direction for build_rail_depot.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "tile": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Tile ID near which to search (use a station tile)"
                        },
                        "radius": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Search radius in tiles (default 10)"
                        },
                        "max_results": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Maximum results to return (default 5)"
                        },
                        "rail_type": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Rail type ID (default 0)"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["tile"]
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.find_rail_depot_spot.FindRailDepotSpot"
        },
        {
            "name": "get_engines",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Gets available train engines and wagons that can be purchased.
Returns: id, name, cargo_label, capacity, max_speed, price,
running_cost, power, weight, reliability, is_wagon.
Locomotives have is_wagon=false, cargo wagons have is_wagon=true.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "vehicle_type": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Vehicle type: 0=train (default), 1=road, 2=ship, 3=aircraft"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.get_engines.GetEngines"
        },
        {
            "name": "get_rail_types",
            "function": {
                "description": "Gets available rail track types. Returns rail type ID, name, and properties.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "include_unavailable": {
                            "type": "boolean",
                            "description": "Include rail types not yet available (default false)"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "rail_mas.get_rail_types.GetRailTypes"
        }
    ]
}
